<title>USA: Mass. home sales jump 13 percent in Q3 - realtors.</title>
<headline>Mass. home sales jump 13 percent in Q3 - realtors.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW YORK, Nov 8 (Reuter) The sale of single-family homes in Massachusetts rose 13 percent during the third quarter of 1996, the state's Association of Realtors said.</p>
<p>The Association said favorable mortgage rates, improved job growth and a modest increase in available housing stock all created a strong demand from first-time and trade-up buyers.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
